  "id": "navigation/call_hierarchy/06_virtual_dispatch",
  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "call_hierarchy",
  "title": "Calls through an override",
  "summary": "A call through a virtual method is an incoming call of every override it may dispatch to; a call through an override is not one of the method it overrides",
  "prose": "`b.draw()` on a `Base&` may run `Base::draw` or `Derived::draw`, so both\nlist it among their incoming calls. `d.draw()` on a `Derived&` runs\n`Derived::draw` or an override below it, never `Base::draw`, so only the\noverride lists it.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
